{"result": {"response": {"id": "chatcmpl-486af00c-bbb7-9b75-a994-8a12d5a872bd", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"content": "{\n    \"title\": \"Antifibrinolytic Drugs and Associated Bleeding/Thrombotic Conditions\",\n    \"summary\": \"This community centers on antifibrinolytic drugs—primarily ammonia-based agents such as 氨甲环酸 (tranexamic acid), 氨甲苯酸 (aminomethylbenzoic acid), and 氨基己酸 (aminocaproic acid)—and their clinical relationships with bleeding disorders, thrombotic side effects, and interacting coagulation factors. These drugs are indicated for conditions involving excessive fibrinolysis, including various hemorrhagic diseases, but carry significant risks of adverse reactions like thrombosis and renal complications. Key coagulation-related entities such as 凝血酶原复合物浓缩剂 (prothrombin complex concentrate) and 凝血因子IX (Factor IX) interact with these drugs, amplifying thrombotic risk.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"氨甲环酸 is a central therapeutic agent with multiple indications and serious adverse effects\",\n            \"explanation\": \"氨甲环酸 (tranexamic acid) emerges as a core entity in this community due to its high degree centrality (31) and extensive relationships. It is clinically indicated for a range of bleeding conditions linked to primary hyperfibrinolysis, including 甲状腺出血 (thyroid hemorrhage) and 原发性纤维蛋白溶解亢进 (primary fibrinolysis hyperactivity). However, it also carries documented risks of severe adverse reactions, notably 颅内血栓形成 (intracranial thrombosis) and 继发性肾盂肾炎 (secondary pyelonephritis), particularly when used in high doses or in susceptible populations. Evidence indicates that drug overdose may lead to central nervous system symptoms and thrombotic events [Data: Entities (6222); Relationships (13014, 21983, 21987, 13022, 13026, +more)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"氨甲苯酸 and 氨基己酸 share similar therapeutic profiles and thrombotic risks\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Both 氨甲苯酸 (degree 19) and 氨基己酸 (degree 16) are antifibrinolytic agents used to manage bleeding associated with hyperfibrinolysis. 氨甲苯酸 is indicated for serious conditions including 严重肝病出血 (severe liver disease–related bleeding), 妇产科意外 (obstetric emergencies), 癌肿 (cancer), and 原发性纤维蛋白溶解过度 (excessive primary fibrinolysis). Similarly, 氨基己酸 is used for diverse hemorrhagic conditions such as 子宫出血 (uterine bleeding), 前列腺出血 (prostate hemorrhage), 尿道出血 (urethral bleeding), 肾上腺出血 (adrenal hemorrhage), and 肝出血 (liver hemorrhage). Critically, both drugs are associated with 血栓形成 (thrombosis) as an adverse reaction, especially when combined with estrogenic compounds or other procoagulant agents [Data: Entities (6224, 6189); Relationships (13027, 22000, 22003, 22001, 22002, +more); Relationships (21944, 21943, 21945, 21948, 21946, 12933)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Drug–drug interactions with coagulation factors significantly increase thrombotic risk\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Several antifibrinolytic drugs exhibit dangerous interactions with procoagulant agents. Specifically, 氨甲环酸 interacts with 凝血酶原复合物浓缩剂 (prothrombin complex concentrate), 凝血因子 (coagulation factors), and 因子Ⅸ (Factor IX), all of which elevate the risk of 血栓形成 (thrombosis). Structured evidence warns that concurrent use should be approached with caution, and some guidelines recommend delaying antifibrinolytic administration by at least 8 hours after coagulation factor infusion. Similar interaction warnings exist between 氨甲苯酸 and 凝血因子IX. These pharmacodynamic synergies create a high-risk profile for patients requiring both hemostatic support and antifibrinolytic therapy [Data: Relationships (41081, 41080, 41082, 41092)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Bleeding conditions treated span multiple organ systems and disease etiologies\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The community encompasses a wide spectrum of hemorrhagic conditions across organ systems, reflecting the broad applicability of antifibrinolytics. These include 脑出血 (intracerebral hemorrhage), 肺出血 (pulmonary hemorrhage), 肝出血 (hepatic hemorrhage), 前列腺出血 (prostatic hemorrhage), 尿道出血 (urethral hemorrhage), 肾上腺出血 (adrenal hemorrhage), and 子宫出血 (uterine bleeding). Additionally, systemic conditions like 弥散性血管内凝血 (disseminated intravascular coagulation, DIC) and 严重肝病出血 (bleeding due to severe liver disease) are represented. This diversity underscores the role of fibrinolysis dysregulation in both localized and systemic bleeding pathologies [Data: Entities (17148, 1964, 1889, 376, 775, 2007, 705, 115, 834); Relationships (21526)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Thrombosis is a recurrent and critical adverse effect across multiple antifibrinolytics\",\n            \"explanation\": \"血栓形成 (thrombosis) appears repeatedly as a serious adverse reaction associated with antifibrinolytic therapy. 氨甲环酸 is linked to 颅内血栓形成 (intracranial thrombosis), while 氨甲苯酸 and 氨基己酸 are both flagged for general thrombosis risk, particularly in patients using hormonal agents. The mechanism involves suppression of fibrinolysis, which—while beneficial for controlling bleeding—can tip the hemostatic balance toward pathological clot formation. Clinical guidance emphasizes vigilant monitoring for thrombotic complications during treatment [Data: Entities (17331, 17692); Relationships (13026, 13027, 12933)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Renal complications are notable adverse effects of antifibrinolytic use\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Beyond thrombosis, renal adverse effects are documented, particularly with 氨甲环酸 and its formulation 注射用氨甲环酸 (injectable tranexamic acid). Both are associated with 继发性肾盂肾炎 (secondary pyelonephritis) and potential 输尿管凝血块阻塞 (ureteral clot obstruction), warranting caution in patients with preexisting urological or renal pathology. Additionally, 氨甲苯酸氯化钠 (aminomethylbenzoic acid sodium chloride) is linked to 急性肾功能衰竭 (acute kidney injury) in the context of thrombotic complications affecting organ perfusion. These findings highlight the need for renal function monitoring during therapy [Data: Entities (16805, 6225); Relationships (13022, 13481, 13028)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Underlying diseases like cancer and leukemia contextualize treatment indications\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Certain systemic diseases serve as underlying etiologies for the bleeding conditions treated with antifibrinolytics. Notably, 癌肿 (cancer) and 白血病 (leukemia) are explicitly cited as contexts in which 原发性纤维蛋白溶解过度 (excessive primary fibrinolysis) occurs, justifying the use of 氨甲苯酸. Interestingly, 白血病 is also listed as a potential adverse reaction to 苯丁酸氮芥 (chlorambucil), though this drug is not otherwise central to the community. This suggests that the community reflects both therapeutic responses to malignancy-associated coagulopathies and iatrogenic risks from other agents [Data: Entities (1597, 16559); Relationships (22004, 15686)].\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 7.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The community poses a high clinical impact due to the life-threatening balance between controlling severe hemorrhage and inducing thrombotic or renal complications.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "created": 1782128649, "model": "qwen3-max", "object": "chat.completion", "moderation": null, "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1957, "prompt_tokens": 7129, "total_tokens": 9086, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 1280}}, "formatted_response": null, "content": "{\n    \"title\": \"Antifibrinolytic Drugs and Associated Bleeding/Thrombotic Conditions\",\n    \"summary\": \"Thi